      "message": "fix(post): the Tormach safe retract comes from the machine file\n\nG53 G0 Z0 is straight up only where machine Z0 is the top of Z travel\n(Tormach's convention); a LinuxCNC machine homed with Z0 at the bottom\nrapids down into the part. The .mch Z part now states `safe_retract`\n(machine coordinates, file unit; mirrored as `safeRetractZ`, mm), every\nshipped Tormach file and the generic VMCs state 0, and tormach.cps\nretracts to the stated Z. A document with no machine or a Tormach model\nstating none keeps Z0 + G30 byte-identical; any other machine stating\nnone is refused by name. A non-zero safe Z drops the PathPilot G30 (an\nunset G30 position is the machine origin) and says so in the header.\n\nFixes #495\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
